# Redoubt isolation-media-drain-backport.patch  (Android, android.txt, 158.0-2)
# Owner: LW-M7-50. BACKPORT of upstream bug 1987001, not Redoubt code.
#
#   Bug 1987001 - Improve draining in FFmpegVideoDecoder and FFmpegAudioDecoder
#   on Android. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski
#   Author: Andrew Osmond <aosmond@mozilla.com>, 2026-10-05
#   mozilla-firefox commit 5cf346157068a285144cfb2f0409e81a2796ac59 (Firefox 159)
#   Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329595
#   Upstream patch sha256 (github.com/.../commit/<sha>.patch, fetched 2026-10-10):
#   8d7cc715260958f792d83a2aa26b3bfb01aa20fef0d4ee19d86683d7f8faa2ec
#
# Unconditional (not behind the Android 12+ runtime gate): it is upstream's
# own code for every Android build from Firefox 159 on.
#
# Why: with isolated content (Android 12+), H.264/AAC decode through ffvpx's NDK MediaCodec
# wrapper. In 158 that wrapper completes a drain while MediaCodec still holds
# frames (an output format change before the first frame, or no free output
# buffer until the compositor releases one), so the last frames of a stream are
# lost and a SHORT clip may show no frame at all (upstream commit message).
# Upstream's own isolated-process configuration (bug 1988531) runs with this fix
# in 159; a 158 dot release with isolation on must carry it too.
#
# On Android 8-11 (isolation off, media prefs as in 158.0-1) its code does not
# run in practice: the video/audio parts act only on a MediaCodec-backed ffvpx
# decoder, which needs media.ffvpx-hw.enabled (false there, its 158.0-1 value);
# the audio decoder no longer re-sends an empty drain packet it already sent
# (158 ended the drain loop on the AVERROR_EOF FFmpeg returns for the second
# one; now the loop ends because that DoDecode() yields no frame, and the drain
# promise resolves with the same frames either way); and the flush/shutdown RejectIfExists() finds no pending drain promise,
# because a software ffvpx drain settles before ProcessDrain() returns. API 30
# --check-video and --check-isolation show the same decoders and playback as
# Beta 2 (docs/android/evidence/lw-m7-50/release-158.0-2/).
#
# Upstream files touched (all six of the upstream commit)
# -------------------------------------------------------
#   dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegAudioDecoder.cpp, .h
#   dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegDataDecoder.cpp, .h
#   dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp, .h
#
# How clean the backport is: 14 of the 15 upstream hunks apply to 158.0 as they
# are (offsets only, one fuzz-1 context line). ONE hunk does not: upstream adds
# `mHasSentDrainPacket = false;` to an FFmpegAudioDecoder::ProcessFlush()
# override that 158.0 does not have (upstream added it in between, for
# mInputTimes, which 158 also lacks). The backport adds that override with only
# the drain reset, declared in the .h; it calls FFmpegDataDecoder::ProcessFlush()
# exactly as upstream's does. Everything is under MOZ_WIDGET_ANDROID and, for
# the decoder-specific parts, a MediaCodec-backed decoder, so the software
# ffvpx paths in content keep their behaviour (a flush or shutdown now also
# rejects a pending drain promise, as upstream does on every platform).
#
# Drop this patch at the Firefox 159 rebase (the fix is upstream there).
#
